P20 is a tripwire over names: a dependency re-exporting the function under
another name escapes it, and so does an alias spelled other than
`name as other` (a `type` or `fn` wrapper).
P22 is a tripwire over names: it sees that the calls are spelled, not that
the barrier's verdict is obeyed (the tpm2 unit tests and the integration
cap-failure boot adjudicate that).
P21 is a fail-closed check of one expression's shape: it reads the tail
expression only, so a `return` earlier in the body escapes it (the review
of the pass order is the adjudicating control).
